{"parentUuid":"46400049-80fe-4d24-919e-93662d2aaba4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"ab2efb1b0554a0078","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016J7m6jNnmzA8dCU4RjuR8Q","type":"tool_result","content":"== cli/reference\n286:### `codex fork`\n288:Fork a previous interactive session into a new chat. By default, `codex fork` opens the session picker; add `--last` to fork your most recent session instead.\n290:When the current and saved session directories differ, `codex fork` uses the\n293:<ConfigTable client:load options={forkOptions} />\n330:- Press <kbd>Escape</kbd> twice with an empty composer to edit the previous user message and fork the chat from that point.\n398:| [`/fork`](#fork-the-current-chat-with-fork)                                                 | Fork the current chat into a new chat.                          | Branch the active session to explore a new approach without losing the current transcript.                 |\n805:<a id=\"fork-the-current-conversation-with-fork\"></a>\n807:### Fork the current chat with `/fork`\n== cli/features\n== noninteractive\n== hooks\n== app-server\n205:- **Start (or resume) a thread**: Call `thread/start` for a new conversation, `thread/resume` to continue an existing one, or `thread/fork` to branch history into a new thread id.\n298:- `thread/fork` - fork a thread into a new thread id by copying stored history. Pass `lastTurnId` to copy history through that turn and omit later turns, or `ephemeral: true` to create an in-memory fork. Emits `thread/started` for the new thread; returned threads include `forkedFromId` when available.\n519:`thread/start`, `thread/resume`, and `thread/fork` return\n537:use their own thread id as the session id; forked threads keep the session id\n597:To branch from a stored session, call `thread/fork` with the `thread.id`. This creates a new thread id and emits a `thread/started` notification for it. Pass\n602:{ \"method\": \"thread/fork\", \"id\": 12, \"params\": { \"threadId\": \"thr_123\", \"lastTurnId\": \"turn_456\" } }\n603:{ \"id\": 12, \"result\": { \"thread\": { \"id\": \"thr_456\", \"sessionId\": \"thr_123\", \"forkedFromId\": \"thr_123\" } } }\n608:source thread is mid-turn, the fork records an interruption marker instead of","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"63083b36-9339-4a88-b1fa-b50d5b4d9843","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:54:39.521Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"46400049-80fe-4d24-919e-93662d2aaba4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab2efb1b0554a0078","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
