t-result/samples/20261003-144618/stream.jsonl (and 21 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The only test (TestStopBlockContinuesTheTurnWithOneEnd) never checks the doc-stated Stop rule that `continue: false` takes precedence over block decisions. Its checks that the reason reaches the agent and the turn goes on are also loose: it only does a Contains on the rollout text and a count of one turn.completed. The recorded 4 agent_message items after the blocks are not asserted, and neither is the continuation prompt being a user-role message.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/subagent_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/agent_calls.go, codex-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/foreground-subagent-result/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/foreground-subagent-result/samples/20261003-144618/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/foreground-subagent-result/samples/20261003-144618/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/foreground-subagent-result/samples/20261003-144618/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/foreground-subagent-result/samples/20261003-144618/payloads.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/foreground-subagent-result/samples/20261003-144618/stderr.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/foreground-subagent-result/samples/20261003-144618/stream.jsonl (and 21 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - TestStopPayloadCarriesLastMessageAndContinuing asserts last_assistant_message only on the first Stop (\"DONE\"). The recording's continued Stops (stop_hook_active:true) carry the new message \"DONE2\", so a mock that repeated the stale message would still pass. It also never checks the doc'd and recorded turn_id field, which is the same across all Stops in a turn. It also never covers the third Stop after an exit-2 block, where stop_hook_active stays true.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/subagent_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/agent_calls.go, codex-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/