{"parentUuid":"c86414db-5dd3-4687-8d7f-dec06954c579","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab2efb1b0554a0078","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffbFiDqSKH9Nn7SQuVzd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I could not push or open a PR. The `verify-before-push` gate blocked `git push`, so nothing is on origin and there is no PR number or merge status. The work is committed locally on branch `worktree-agent-ab2efb1b0554a0078`.\n\nThe gate wants a clean `sr-checks` run on HEAD. My last full run, after the rebase, refused only on other capabilities' cells. None of the refusals names session-fork or session-start-hook. These are mostly codex and cursor hook cells, such as `posttooluse-payload/codex` and `hook-matcher-filter/cursor`. They get re-judged because my change touches shared snapshot files like `MANIFEST.yaml`, `capture.sh` and `run.go`, and fixing them would mean rewriting other capabilities' cells. I did not re-run the exact `--base 41ae6c6` command the gate printed. I expect the same result, and each full run takes about 20 minutes.\n\nDecision for you: either accept the unrelated refusals and push past the gate, or tell me to fix those other cells; I stopped rather than do either.\n\n**codex × session-fork: supported.**\n- **Run:** `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork`. It records an original session, then `codex exec fork <id>`, then `codex exec resume <id>`.\n- **What the recording shows:** the fork gets a new session id and fires SessionStart with source \"fork\". The agent answered \"ORIGINAL\", so it continued the conversation. The fork's rollout does not copy the history; its meta record points at the original via `forked_from_id` and `history_base`.\n- **Mock:** it now handles `exec fork <id> [prompt]`. The new code is in `codex-mock/internal/session/fork.go`, tagged `sr:provides session-fork/codex`, with a small additive core helper in `internal/session/fork_base.go`.\n- **Tests:** two in `codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/session_fork_test.go`. One is marked `sr:proves session-fork/codex` and one `sr:proves session-start-hook/codex`. The e2e tests I ran pass.\n- **Deviations declared in the cell:**\n  - Codex's fork keeps history by reference rather than copying it.\n  - Only `exec fork` is modeled; interactive `codex fork` and `/fork` are not.\n  - The scripted agent in the mock cannot see the earlier conversation.\n- **Docs cited:** `https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/reference#codex-fork`, newly frozen in the MANIFEST.\n\n**cursor × session-fork: unsupported.**\n- **Run:** `cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork`. `--resume <id>` kept the same session id and a single transcript, and `--fork` failed with \"unknown option '--fork'\" and exit 1.\n- **Docs cited:** `https://cursor.com/docs/cli/reference/parameters#global-options`, newly frozen. There are no markers for this cell.\n\nI made two changes you did not ask for:\n- **`session-start-hook` cell:** I edited the codex cell's deviation text, which said the mock never forks. That became false once `exec fork` landed.\n- **`capture.sh` steps:** both `capture.sh` scripts now accept later steps as flat files, `then-NN-prompt.txt` and so on. The structure gate blocks subdirectories under `setup/`. Other session-resume agents may add something similar, so expect merge conflicts there.\n\nThe installed `cursor-agent` auto-updated to 2026.10.01 partway through. I recorded with the pinned 2026.09.28 through a wrapper in my scratchpad so the MANIFEST version stays consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1579,"cache_read_input_tokens":214544,"output_tokens":1509,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":273},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1579},"inference_geo":"not_available","