uns/session-fork/samples/20261003-145349/payloads.jsonl (and 30 more) (file-guard \"ca\n76-  - The deviation says the fork's session_meta records how much of the original it was forked from, and the recording shows forked_from_ordinal_exclusive:22 and history_base.end_ordinal_exclusive:22 (end_byte_offset 40280). TestForkContinuesTheConversationUnderANewSessionAndLeavesTheOriginal only asserts forked_from_id and history_base.thread_id, so no test checks the amount of history the fork points at.\n77-The files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/session_fork_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go, codex-mock/internal/session/file.go, codex-mock/internal/session/fork.go, codex-mock/snapshots/capture.sh, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork/samples/20261003-145349/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork/samples/20261003-145349/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork/samples/20261003-145349/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork/samples/20261003-145349/payloads.jsonl (and 30 more) (file-guard \"ca\n78-  - The docs name SessionStart sources resume and compact (hooks#sessionstart), and the compact path is documented in detail: matching hooks run before the next model request, and continue:false ends the turn. The deviation says the mock never resumes or compacts, but the mock does both: codex-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go fires SessionStart with source \"compact\", and internal/session/resume.go exists. The recorded session-fork run also shows a SessionStart with source \"resume\". No test marked sr:proves session-start-hook/codex checks the compact or resume source, only startup and\n79-The files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/session_fork_test.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go, codex-mock/internal/session/file.go, codex-mock/internal/session/fork.go, codex-mock/snapshots/capture.sh, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork/run.yaml, codex-mock/snaps