{"parentUuid":"d58f1bee-f5b9-4fd9-aad9-d669fa04da2f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab2efb1b0554a0078","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffqVmVonrKbPakxMwayh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The last `sr-checks` run refused on three items, all tied to my change:\n- **`session-start-hook` deviation:** it overclaimed. The mock does emit `compact`, and a `resume` start appears in the recording. I rewrote it to say the mock reports `startup`, `fork` and `compact`, and not `resume` or `clear`.\n- **Fork test:** it didn't check how much of the original history the fork points at. It now asserts that `forked_from_ordinal_exclusive` equals `history_base.end_ordinal_exclusive`, and in the mock equals the original rollout's record count at the fork. It passes.\n- **`noninteractive-run/codex`:** it still refuses on `Run` in `codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go`, which I edited, even after #121. It complains about untested doc behaviours such as `--output-schema` and the git-repo check. I haven't touched it. If it remains in the next run, I'll name that pair in my report.\n\nI've committed the two fixes and started `sr-checks run --base origin/main --head HEAD` again in the background. I'll read it when it finishes, then push, open the PR and admin-merge once CI passes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":820,"cache_read_input_tokens":277588,"output_tokens":385,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":820},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":385,"cache_read_input_tokens":277588,"cache_creation_input_tokens":820,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":820,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"