{"parentUuid":"e3879583-56dd-4536-b2e1-59c2804c092c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab2efb1b0554a0078","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffqgpYvVs8U1EMwbWVWw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The branch is still not pushed and has no PR. The push gate still needs a clean `sr-checks` run, and one refusal can't be cleared without your decision.\n\n- **`noninteractive-run/codex`:** it refuses on `Run` in `codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go`, which I edited for the fork wiring. The judge now cites untested doc behaviours: `--output-schema` is accepted but has no effect, and the git-repo-required check is never enforced or tested.\n- **`session-start-hook/codex`:** this one was my own overclaim. I had added \"the mock reports `compact`\" to the deviation, and no test marked for that capability proves it. I cut the sentence so it only says what the mock leaves out (no `resume` or `clear` source), and committed. I haven't re-run `sr-checks` since that commit.\n\nI did not revert the `run.go` edit you asked for, because I can't wire the fork without it. `Run` creates its own session id, calls `session.Create`, and hardcodes `\"startup\"` as the SessionStart source. Nothing in `exec.go` or the session package changes any of those. The only workaround is a package-level override in the shared hooks invoker, which other capabilities read, so I didn't take it. My edit to `Run` is nine lines.\n\nI need one of these from you:\n1. Accept that `noninteractive-run/codex` is re-judged on `Run` and have its debt agent cover `--output-schema` and the git-repo check, or declare them as deviations.\n2. Move the `sr:provides noninteractive-run/codex` marker off `Run`.\n3. Authorize the invoker-level override, accepting the extra re-judging.\n\nThe rebased work is committed locally on `worktree-agent-ab2efb1b0554a0078`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache