{"parentUuid":"c4dee491-0351-48a6-8f20-e8af46a31801","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"ab2efb1b0554a0078","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011tMqyDT1NNdCyjr4UtANiZ","type":"tool_result","content":"67:the following rules refused this work:\n68-  - capability-once: internal/session/fork_base.go adds session-fork behaviour (HistoryBase, ForkBase, Through) in core without the `// sr:capability session-fork` marker, which the Decision requires (\"A capability's behaviour lives once, in `internal/`, on code marked `// sr:capability <id>`\"); mark it (or fold it into the marked Fork), and drop the unused Through. (file-guard \"adr-conformance\")\n69-  - The docs (hooks#sessionstart) name source \"compact\" and the mock fires SessionStart with source \"compact\" (internal/runner/control_compact.go), but the deviation covers only resume and clear and none of this subject's tests (capabilities_test.go, lifecycle_recorded_test.go, session_fork_test.go) asserts the compact source. The compact matcher cases there only check that a hook does NOT run on a fresh start. The only compact-source assertion is in compaction_test.go, which is marked for manual-compaction/codex. Also untested for the compact source: the doc line that continue:false from t\n70-The files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/session_fork_test.go, codex-mock/exec.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/run.go, codex-mock/internal/session/file.go, codex-mock/internal/session/fork.go, codex-mock/snapshots/capture.sh, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork/samples/20261003-145349/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork/samples/20261003-145349/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork/samples/20261003-145349/exit.txt (and 31 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\nFINISHED\n\n[exited with code 0]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a0396b3b-f222-4c82-bca4-c6fcf8295235",