{"parentUuid":"e04ffd97-5bcd-4cc9-9c60-16e6d3b483de","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"ab2efb1b0554a0078","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F7wQvdfspGRWXh2atwUnoD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tstatement: >-\n2\t  A session can be forked when resumed: the fork continues the conversation\n3\t  under a new session id in a new transcript that carries the history, and the\n4\t  original is left untouched.\n5\tproviders:\n6\t  claude:\n7\t    docs:\n8\t      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference#cli-flags\n9\t      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/sessions#fork-to-explore-alternatives\n10\t    runs:\n11\t      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/forkresume\n12\t<<<<<<< HEAD\n13\t      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/resume-continue-fork\n14\t    deviations:\n15\t      - adr: modeled-surface\n16\t        statement: >-\n17\t          The init frame at a session's start and the result frame that ends it,\n18\t          which in the recorded runs name the fork's new session id, are the\n19\t          scenario script's own in the mock, which writes neither (it writes an\n20\t          init frame only after a compaction). The frames the mock writes itself\n21\t          (the SessionStart hook's, a task's, a compaction's) carry the fork's id.\n22\t  codex: pending\n23\t  cursor: pending\n24\t=======\n25\t  codex:\n26\t    docs:"}]},"uuid":"3dbab1bf-3967-445a-8470-9c77731c0fe6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:32:04.297Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e04ffd97-5bcd-4cc9-9c60-16e6d3b483de","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab2efb1b0554a0078","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a5742d151ebfb6c56"}
