{"parentUuid":"0c8d292b-6515-47f1-abf4-8fe525123e07","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab2efb1b0554a0078","attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab2efb1b0554a0078/spec/capabilities/session-start-hook.yaml","snippet":"22\t  codex:\n23\t    docs:\n24\t      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#sessionstart\n25\t    runs:\n26\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n27\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n28\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-matchers\n29\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-continue-false\n30\t<<<<<<< HEAD\n31\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-compact-continue-false\n32\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto\n33\t=======\n34\t>>>>>>> ddda03f8 (session-start-hook: codex cell cites runs/session-fork for the fork start)\n35\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork\n36\t    deviations:\n37\t      - adr: modeled-surface\n38\t        statement: >-\n39\t          The mock never clears a session (the source clear), so a session start is the fresh one, source startup, the one after a compaction, source compact, the one a session resumed by its id (`exec resume`) makes, source resume, or the one `exec fork` makes, source fork (recorded: runs/session-fork).\n40\t      - adr: capability-grounding\n41\t        statement: >-\n42\t          Unlike the statement, a Codex SessionStart hook can stop the run: one"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ba0d1c3c-fdad-40f5-a899-a3120fb54429","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:33:01.426Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab2efb1b0554a0078/spec/capabilities/session-start-hook.yaml changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n22\t  codex:\n23\t    docs:\n24\t      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#sessionstart\n25\t    runs:\n26\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n27\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n28\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-matchers\n29\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-continue-false\n30\t<<<<<<< HEAD\n31\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-compact-continue-false\n32\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto\n33\t=======\n34\t>>>>>>> ddda03f8 (session-start-hook: codex cell cites runs/session-fork for the fork start)\n35\t      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-fork\n36\t    deviations:\n37\t      - adr: modeled-surface\n38\t        statement: >-\n39\t          The mock never clears a session (the source clear), so a session start is the fresh one, source startup, the one after a compaction, source compact, the one a session resumed by its id (`exec resume`) makes, source resume, or the one `exec fork` makes, source fork (recorded: runs/session-fork).\n40\t      - adr: capability-grounding\n41\t        statement: >-\n42\t          Unlike the statement, a Codex SessionStart hook can stop the run: one\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab2efb1b0554a0078","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a5742d151ebfb6c56"}
