{"parentUuid":"bea62b58-7ea2-40d1-9c67-9d5f1cfaaf89","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab2efb1b0554a0078","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffwwM3KLGyhmamvwm9zn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've rebased onto origin/main with #137 and #132 in it and resolved every conflict, keeping both sides:\n\n- **Fork wiring:** it now goes through a new `session.Start` in `codex-mock/internal/session/start.go`, which calls the existing `Begin` for resume. `Run` changed in a few lines, and `Begin` is untouched.\n- **Capture convention:** I dropped my own `then-NN` step handling and took upstream's identical convention. My scenarios now use `<SESSION>` and `resume`/`fork` in the args files.\n- **Re-recorded runs:** I re-recorded both `session-fork` runs under that convention. Codex gives OK, ORIGINAL, RESUMED. Cursor shows resume then \"unknown option '--fork'\".\n- **Spec cells:** the `session-fork` and `session-start-hook` cells now hold both sides. The codex start deviation says the mock reports the `fork` source and the `resume` source and doesn't clear.\n- **Compact test:** I removed my own compact-source test, since #137 now covers that.\n\nBuild, vet and the codex e2e and internal tests pass on the rebased branch. I've started `sr-checks run --base origin/main --head HEAD` in the background and will read it when it finishes. If it's clean, I'll run the gate's exact SHA command, push, open the PR, wait for CI to report and admin-merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":897,"cache_read_input_tokens":369432,"output_tokens":464,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":897},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_to